      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence defines biological aging as “the age-related change in how an organism functions,” but the packet text does not provide this definitional phrasing or a direct statement that biological aging is defined in those terms.",
        "The definition’s specific examples (“declines in movement and memory or learning over the lifespan”) are largely consistent with the packet’s findings, but the packet focuses on particular behaviors in male Drosophila (e.g., climbing speed, courtship performance, courtship memory, short-term memory) rather than presenting a general definition spanning “how an organism functions.”",
